wasm jit: a continuation block for every CALL_HANDLER; bail reasons by gate (gex)

The emitter runs a finally as "finally_ind = continuation block; goto handler", so the
continuation must start a block. Out-of-SSA puts phi moves between a CALL_HANDLER and the
leave's OP_BR, and branch optimization deletes a BR to the fallthrough block; both were refused
as "finally: complex call_handler continuation" (tk2dSprite.UpdateMaterial and
GUILayoutGroup.CalcHeight in Hollow Knight; UnmanagedMemoryStream.ReadByte,
SR.InternalGetResourceString, the resource readers in the BCL). wj_split_call_handler_blocks
moves the instructions after a CALL_HANDLER into a new block reached by an OP_BR, with the
non-handler CFG edges, before any analysis; a CALL_HANDLER that ends its block continues at
bb->next_bb. cfg->num_bblocks stays as it is: it sizes cfg->bblocks, which mono_free_loop_info
walks at mono_destroy_compile (bumping it read past the array and crashed at random).

[wasm-jit bails] also lists every non-opcode gate string with its count and the first method
it refused ("why N gate (first: ...)"), so "synchronized/other" names its reasons.
Tests: T.NestedFinally (FinMove, SrLike, SrLike2, UmsLike, UmsRead).

